    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 102.98,
      "end": 105.54,
      "textEn": "It may be hard to see the roots of modern English",
      "textKo": "현대 영어의 뿌리를 찾기가 어려울 수 있습니다.",
      "words": [{"word": "It", "start": 102.72, "end": 103.06}, {"word": "may", "start": 103.06, "end": 103.18}, {"word": "be", "start": 103.18, "end": 103.34}, {"word": "hard", "start": 103.34, "end": 103.64}, {"word": "to", "start": 103.64, "end": 103.86}, {"word": "see", "start": 103.86, "end": 104.08}, {"word": "the", "start": 104.08, "end": 104.26}, {"word": "roots", "start": 104.26, "end": 104.56}, {"word": "of", "start": 104.56, "end": 104.74}, {"word": "modern", "start": 104.74, "end": 105.04}, {"word": "English", "start": 105.04, "end": 105.54}]
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 105.54,
      "end": 111.2,
      "textEn": "Underneath all the words borrowed from French, Latin, Old Norse, and other languages.",
      "textKo": "프랑스어, 라틴어, 고대 노르드어, 그리고 다른 언어들에서 차용된 모든 단어들 아래에서.",
      "words": [{"word": "underneath", "start": 105.54, "end": 106.16}, {"word": "all", "start": 106.16, "end": 106.64}, {"word": "the", "start": 106.64, "end": 106.82}, {"word": "words", "start": 106.82, "end": 107.18}, {"word": "borrowed", "start": 107.18, "end": 107.58}, {"word": "from", "start": 107.58, "end": 107.82}, {"word": "French,", "start": 107.82, "end": 108.26}, {"word": "Latin,", "start": 108.56, "end": 108.92}, {"word": "Old", "start": 109.26, "end": 109.58}, {"word": "Norse,", "start": 109.58, "end": 110.06}, {"word": "and", "start": 110.16, "end": 110.44}, {"word": "other", "start": 110.44, "end": 110.74}, {"word": "languages.", "start": 110.74, "end": 111.2}]
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 111.5,
      "end": 116.56,
      "textEn": "But comparative linguistics can help us by focusing on grammatical structure,",
      "textKo": "하지만 비교언어학이 문법 구조에 초점을 맞춤으로써 도움을 줄 수 있습니다.",
      "words": [{"word": "But", "start": 111.5, "end": 112.04}, {"word": "comparative", "start": 112.04, "end": 112.66}, {"word": "linguistics", "start": 112.66, "end": 113.38}, {"word": "can", "start": 113.38, "end": 113.84}, {"word": "help", "start": 113.84, "end": 114.1}, {"word": "us", "start": 114.1, "end": 114.34}, {"word": "by", "start": 114.34, "end": 114.54}, {"word": "focusing", "start": 114.54, "end": 115.06}, {"word": "on", "start": 115.06, "end": 115.44}, {"word": "grammatical", "start": 115.44, "end": 116.08}, {"word": "structure,", "start": 116.08, "end": 116.56}]
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 116.56,
      "end": 120.44,
      "textEn": "Patterns of sound changes, and certain core vocabulary.",
      "textKo": "음운 변화의 패턴과 특정 핵심 어휘에 주목함으로써요.",
      "words": [{"word": "patterns", "start": 116.56, "end": 117.32}, {"word": "of", "start": 117.32, "end": 117.52}, {"word": "sound", "start": 117.52, "end": 117.84}, {"word": "changes,", "start": 117.84, "end": 118.3}, {"word": "and", "start": 118.54, "end": 118.86}, {"word": "certain", "start": 118.86, "end": 119.26}, {"word": "core", "start": 119.26, "end": 119.72}, {"word": "vocabulary.", "start": 119.72, "end": 120.44}]
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 120.9,
      "end": 125.44,
      "textEn": "For example, after the 6th century, German words starting with P",
      "textKo": "예를 들어, 6세기 이후에 P로 시작하는 독일어 단어들은",
      "words": [{"word": "For", "start": 120.9, "end": 121.36}, {"word": "example,", "start": 121.36, "end": 121.74}, {"word": "after", "start": 122.22, "end": 122.5}, {"word": "the", "start": 122.5, "end": 122.68}, {"word": "6th", "start": 122.68, "end": 123.02}, {"word": "century,", "start": 123.02, "end": 123.4}, {"word": "German", "start": 123.76, "end": 124.14}, {"word": "words", "start": 124.14, "end": 124.56}, {"word": "starting", "start": 124.56, "end": 124.92}, {"word": "with", "start": 124.92, "end": 125.16}, {"word": "P", "start": 125.16, "end": 125.44}]
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 125.44,
      "end": 128.36,
      "textEn": "Systematically shifted to a PF sound,",
      "textKo": "체계적으로 PF 소리로 변했지만,",
      "words": [{"word": "systematically", "start": 125.44, "end": 126.36}, {"word": "shifted", "start": 126.36, "end": 127.06}, {"word": "to", "start": 127.06, "end": 127.32}, {"word": "a", "start": 127.32, "end": 127.5}, {"word": "PF", "start": 127.5, "end": 127.9}, {"word": "sound,", "start": 127.9, "end": 128.36}]
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 128.56,
      "end": 132.12,
      "textEn": "While their Old English counterparts kept the P unchanged.",
      "textKo": "고대 영어의 대응어들은 P를 그대로 유지했습니다.",
      "words": [{"word": "while", "start": 128.56, "end": 129.0}, {"word": "their", "start": 129.0, "end": 129.18}, {"word": "Old", "start": 129.18, "end": 129.42}, {"word": "English", "start": 129.42, "end": 129.78}, {"word": "counterparts", "start": 129.78, "end": 130.32}, {"word": "kept", "start": 130.32, "end": 131.0}, {"word": "the", "start": 131.0, "end": 131.22}, {"word": "P", "start": 131.22, "end": 131.42}, {"word": "unchanged.", "start": 131.42, "end": 132.12}]
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 132.9,
      "end": 139.72,
      "textEn": "In another split, words that have SK sounds in Swedish developed an SH sound in English.",
      "textKo": "또 다른 분리에서는, 스웨덴어에서 SK 소리를 가진 단어들이 영어에서 SH 소리로 발전했습니다.",
      "words": [{"word": "In", "start": 132.9, "end": 133.2}, {"word": "another", "start": 133.2, "end": 133.48}, {"word": "split,", "start": 133.48, "end": 133.84}, {"word": "words", "start": 134.2, "end": 134.6}, {"word": "that", "start": 134.6, "end": 134.74}, {"word": "have", "start": 134.74, "end": 135.02}, {"word": "SK", "start": 135.02, "end": 135.52}, {"word": "sounds", "start": 135.52, "end": 136.08}, {"word": "in", "start": 136.08, "end": 136.36}, {"word": "Swedish", "start": 136.36, "end": 136.86}, {"word": "developed", "start": 136.86, "end": 137.7}, {"word": "an", "start": 137.7, "end": 137.96}, {"word": "SH", "start": 137.96, "end": 138.34}, {"word": "sound", "start": 138.34, "end": 138.9}, {"word": "in", "start": 138.9, "end": 139.34}, {"word": "English.", "start": 139.34, "end": 139.72}]
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 140.18,
      "end": 144.62,
      "textEn": "There are still some English words with SK, like skirt and skull,",
      "textKo": "skirt(치마)와 skull(두개골)처럼 SK가 있는 영어 단어들이 여전히 일부 있지만,",
      "words": [{"word": "There", "start": 140.18, "end": 140.68}, {"word": "are", "start": 140.68, "end": 140.84}, {"word": "still", "start": 140.84, "end": 141.06}, {"word": "some", "start": 141.06, "end": 141.34}, {"word": "English", "start": 141.34, "end": 141.62}, {"word": "words", "start": 141.62, "end": 142.0}, {"word": "with", "start": 142.0, "end": 142.22}, {"word": "SK,", "start": 142.22, "end": 142.7}, {"word": "like", "start": 143.08, "end": 143.36}, {"word": "skirt", "start": 143.36, "end": 143.74}, {"word": "and", "start": 143.74, "end": 144.22}, {"word": "skull,", "start": 144.22, "end": 144.62}]
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 144.62,
      "end": 151.22,
      "textEn": "But they're direct borrowings from Old Norse that came after the SK to SH shift.",
      "textKo": "그것들은 SK에서 SH로의 변화 이후에 들어온 고대 노르드어에서의 직접적인 차용어입니다.",
      "words": [{"word": "but", "start": 144.62, "end": 145.3}, {"word": "they're", "start": 145.3, "end": 145.58}, {"word": "direct", "start": 145.58, "end": 146.08}, {"word": "borrowings", "start": 146.08, "end": 146.8}, {"word": "from", "start": 146.8, "end": 147.04}, {"word": "Old", "start": 147.04, "end": 147.3}, {"word": "Norse", "start": 147.3, "end": 147.82}, {"word": "that", "start": 147.82, "end": 148.16}, {"word": "came", "start": 148.16, "end": 148.48}, {"word": "after", "start": 148.48, "end": 149.06}, {"word": "the", "start": 149.06, "end": 149.34}, {"word": "SK", "start": 149.34, "end": 149.78}, {"word": "to", "start": 149.78, "end": 150.1}, {"word": "SH", "start": 150.1, "end": 150.6}, {"word": "shift.", "start": 150.6, "end": 151.22}]
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 151.9,
      "end": 157.38,
      "textEn": "These examples show us that just as the various Romance languages descended from Latin,",
      "textKo": "이러한 예들은 다양한 로망스어들이 라틴어에서 파생된 것처럼,",
      "words": [{"word": "These", "start": 151.9, "end": 152.54}, {"word": "examples", "start": 152.54, "end": 152.96}, {"word": "show", "start": 152.96, "end": 153.3}, {"word": "us", "start": 153.3, "end": 153.58}, {"word": "that", "start": 153.58, "end": 153.96}, {"word": "just", "start": 153.96, "end": 154.26}, {"word": "as", "start": 154.26, "end": 154.54}, {"word": "the", "start": 154.54, "end": 154.68}, {"word": "various", "start": 154.68, "end": 155.12}, {"word": "Romance", "start": 155.12, "end": 155.76}, {"word": "languages", "start": 155.76, "end": 156.18}, {"word": "descended", "start": 156.18, "end": 156.72}, {"word": "from", "start": 156.72, "end": 157.02}, {"word": "Latin,", "start": 157.02, "end": 157.38}]
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 157.82,
      "end": 161.32,
      "textEn": "English, Swedish, German, and many other languages",
      "textKo": "영어, 스웨덴어, 독일어, 그리고 많은 다른 언어들도",
      "words": [{"word": "English,", "start": 157.82, "end": 158.3}, {"word": "Swedish,", "start": 158.56, "end": 159.02}, {"word": "German,", "start": 159.44, "end": 159.88}, {"word": "and", "start": 160.06, "end": 160.3}, {"word": "many", "start": 160.3, "end": 160.52}, {"word": "other", "start": 160.52, "end": 160.82}, {"word": "languages", "start": 160.82, "end": 161.32}]
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 161.32,
      "end": 168.1,
      "textEn": "Descended from their own common ancestor, known as Proto-Germanic, spoken around 500 BCE.",
      "textKo": "기원전 500년경에 사용된 원시 게르만어라고 알려진 공통 조상에서 파생되었습니다.",
      "words": [{"word": "descended", "start": 161.32, "end": 162.12}, {"word": "from", "start": 162.12, "end": 162.4}, {"word": "their", "start": 162.4, "end": 162.56}, {"word": "own", "start": 162.56, "end": 162.82}, {"word": "common", "start": 162.82, "end": 163.14}, {"word": "ancestor,", "start": 163.14, "end": 163.74}, {"word": "known", "start": 164.0, "end": 164.36}, {"word": "as", "start": 164.36, "end": 164.66}, {"word": "Proto", "start": 164.66, "end": 165.14}, {"word": "-Germanic,", "start": 165.14, "end": 165.76}, {"word": "spoken", "start": 165.86, "end": 166.38}, {"word": "around", "start": 166.38, "end": 166.78}, {"word": "500", "start": 166.78, "end": 167.46}, {"word": "BCE.", "start": 167.46, "end": 168.1}]
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 168.78,
      "end": 171.98,
      "textEn": "Because this historical language was never written down,",
      "textKo": "이 역사적 언어는 문자로 기록된 적이 없기 때문에,",
      "words": [{"word": "Because", "start": 168.78, "end": 169.54}, {"word": "this", "start": 169.54, "end": 169.76}, {"word": "historical", "start": 169.76, "end": 170.28}, {"word": "language", "start": 170.28, "end": 170.74}, {"word": "was", "start": 170.74, "end": 171.02}, {"word": "never", "start": 171.02, "end": 171.3}, {"word": "written", "start": 171.3, "end": 171.6}, {"word": "down,", "start": 171.6, "end": 171.98}]
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 171.98,
      "end": 175.6,
      "textEn": "We can only reconstruct it by comparing its descendants,",
      "textKo": "우리는 그 후손 언어들을 비교함으로써만 재구성할 수 있으며,",
      "words": [{"word": "we", "start": 171.98, "end": 172.5}, {"word": "can", "start": 172.5, "end": 172.66}, {"word": "only", "start": 172.66, "end": 172.98}, {"word": "reconstruct", "start": 172.98, "end": 173.58}, {"word": "it", "start": 173.58, "end": 173.9}, {"word": "by", "start": 173.9, "end": 174.28}, {"word": "comparing", "start": 174.28, "end": 174.78}, {"word": "its", "start": 174.78, "end": 175.1}, {"word": "descendants,", "start": 175.1, "end": 175.6}]
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 175.96,
      "end": 178.88,
      "textEn": "Which is possible thanks to the consistency of the changes.",
      "textKo": "이는 변화의 일관성 덕분에 가능합니다.",
      "words": [{"word": "which", "start": 175.96, "end": 176.3}, {"word": "is", "start": 176.3, "end": 176.42}, {"word": "possible", "start": 176.42, "end": 176.9}, {"word": "thanks", "start": 176.9, "end": 177.24}, {"word": "to", "start": 177.24, "end": 177.44}, {"word": "the", "start": 177.44, "end": 177.54}, {"word": "consistency", "start": 177.54, "end": 178.12}, {"word": "of", "start": 178.12, "end": 178.44}, {"word": "the", "start": 178.44, "end": 178.54}, {"word": "changes.", "start": 178.54, "end": 178.88}]
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 179.2,
      "end": 183.32,
      "textEn": "We can even use the same process to go back one step further",
      "textKo": "우리는 같은 과정을 사용하여 한 단계 더 거슬러 올라갈 수도 있고,",
      "words": [{"word": "We", "start": 179.2, "end": 179.84}, {"word": "can", "start": 179.84, "end": 179.98}, {"word": "even", "start": 179.98, "end": 180.22}, {"word": "use", "start": 180.22, "end": 180.52}, {"word": "the", "start": 180.52, "end": 180.7}, {"word": "same", "start": 180.7, "end": 180.94}, {"word": "process", "start": 180.94, "end": 181.4}, {"word": "to", "start": 181.4, "end": 181.7}, {"word": "go", "start": 181.7, "end": 181.86}, {"word": "back", "start": 181.86, "end": 182.08}, {"word": "one", "start": 182.08, "end": 182.42}, {"word": "step", "start": 182.42, "end": 182.8}, {"word": "further", "start": 182.8, "end": 183.32}]
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 183.32,
      "end": 189.16,
      "textEn": "And trace the origins of Proto-Germanic to a language called Proto-Indo-European,",
      "textKo": "원시 게르만어의 기원을 인도유럽조어라는 언어까지 추적할 수 있습니다.",
      "words": [{"word": "and", "start": 183.32, "end": 183.88}, {"word": "trace", "start": 183.88, "end": 184.18}, {"word": "the", "start": 184.18, "end": 184.38}, {"word": "origins", "start": 184.38, "end": 184.9}, {"word": "of", "start": 184.9, "end": 185.2}, {"word": "Proto", "start": 185.2, "end": 185.58}, {"word": "-Germanic", "start": 185.58, "end": 186.18}, {"word": "to", "start": 186.18, "end": 186.6}, {"word": "a", "start": 186.6, "end": 186.74}, {"word": "language", "start": 186.74, "end": 187.12}, {"word": "called", "start": 187.12, "end": 187.48}, {"word": "Proto", "start": 187.48, "end": 188.06}, {"word": "-Indo", "start": 188.06, "end": 188.52}, {"word": "-European,", "start": 188.52, "end": 189.16}]
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 189.24,
      "end": 195.62,
      "textEn": "Spoken about 6,000 years ago on the Pontic Steppe in modern-day Ukraine and Russia.",
      "textKo": "약 6,000년 전 현재의 우크라이나와 러시아에 있는 폰투스 초원에서 사용되었습니다.",
      "words": [{"word": "spoken", "start": 189.24, "end": 190.02}, {"word": "about", "start": 190.02, "end": 190.3}, {"word": "6", "start": 190.3, "end": 190.62}, {"word": ",000", "start": 190.62, "end": 191.16}, {"word": "years", "start": 191.16, "end": 191.38}, {"word": "ago", "start": 191.38, "end": 191.72}, {"word": "on", "start": 191.72, "end": 192.2}, {"word": "the", "start": 192.2, "end": 192.38}, {"word": "Pontic", "start": 192.38, "end": 192.78}, {"word": "Steppe", "start": 192.78, "end": 193.24}, {"word": "in", "start": 193.24, "end": 193.7}, {"word": "modern", "start": 193.7, "end": 194.04}, {"word": "-day", "start": 194.04, "end": 194.3}, {"word": "Ukraine", "start": 194.3, "end": 194.92}, {"word": "and", "start": 194.92, "end": 195.28}, {"word": "Russia.", "start": 195.28, "end": 195.62}]
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 195.62,
      "end": 200.32,
      "textEn": "This is the reconstructed ancestor of the Indo-European family",
      "textKo": "이것은 인도유럽어족의 재구성된 조상 언어로,",
      "words": [{"word": "This", "start": 195.62, "end": 196.46}, {"word": "is", "start": 196.46, "end": 196.64}, {"word": "the", "start": 196.64, "end": 196.78}, {"word": "reconstructed", "start": 196.78, "end": 197.58}, {"word": "ancestor", "start": 197.58, "end": 198.26}, {"word": "of", "start": 198.26, "end": 198.8}, {"word": "the", "start": 198.8, "end": 198.94}, {"word": "Indo", "start": 198.94, "end": 199.26}, {"word": "-European", "start": 199.26, "end": 199.9}, {"word": "family", "start": 199.9, "end": 200.32}]
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 200.32,
      "end": 204.64,
      "textEn": "That includes nearly all languages historically spoken in Europe,",
      "textKo": "역사적으로 유럽에서 사용된 거의 모든 언어를 포함하며,",
      "words": [{"word": "that", "start": 200.32, "end": 200.82}, {"word": "includes", "start": 200.82, "end": 201.26}, {"word": "nearly", "start": 201.26, "end": 201.58}, {"word": "all", "start": 201.58, "end": 201.98}, {"word": "languages", "start": 201.98, "end": 202.56}, {"word": "historically", "start": 202.56, "end": 203.46}, {"word": "spoken", "start": 203.46, "end": 203.96}, {"word": "in", "start": 203.96, "end": 204.3}, {"word": "Europe,", "start": 204.3, "end": 204.64}]
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 204.9,
      "end": 208.0,
      "textEn": "As well as large parts of southern and western Asia.",
      "textKo": "남아시아와 서아시아의 대부분 지역의 언어도 포함합니다.",
      "words": [{"word": "as", "start": 204.9, "end": 205.34}, {"word": "well", "start": 205.34, "end": 205.44}, {"word": "as", "start": 205.44, "end": 205.64}, {"word": "large", "start": 205.64, "end": 205.88}, {"word": "parts", "start": 205.88, "end": 206.26}, {"word": "of", "start": 206.26, "end": 206.46}, {"word": "southern", "start": 206.46, "end": 206.8}, {"word": "and", "start": 206.8, "end": 207.08}, {"word": "western", "start": 207.08, "end": 207.44}, {"word": "Asia.", "start": 207.44, "end": 208.0}]
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 208.46,
      "end": 211.2,
      "textEn": "And though it requires a bit more work,",
      "textKo": "좀 더 많은 작업이 필요하지만,",
      "words": [{"word": "And", "start": 208.46, "end": 209.2}, {"word": "though", "start": 209.2, "end": 209.36}, {"word": "it", "start": 209.36, "end": 209.52}, {"word": "requires", "start": 209.52, "end": 210.0}, {"word": "a", "start": 210.0, "end": 210.26}, {"word": "bit", "start": 210.26, "end": 210.5}, {"word": "more", "start": 210.5, "end": 210.8}, {"word": "work,", "start": 210.8, "end": 211.2}]
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 211.48,
      "end": 215.58,
      "textEn": "We can find the same systematic similarities, or correspondences,",
      "textKo": "같은 체계적인 유사점, 즉 대응 관계를 찾을 수 있습니다.",
